import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy and analytics" description="How kokoapi.space processes files and measures aggregate pageviews.">
  <section class="container home-block" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <p class="section-index">PRIVACY / MEASUREMENT</p>
    <h1 id="privacy-title">Files stay local. Audience metrics stay aggregate.</h1>
    <p class="lead">PDF, image, conversion and Repasses file contents are processed in your browser. They are not sent to the analytics service.</p>

    <h2>What we measure</h2>
    <p>Our self-hosted analytics counts pageviews and groups them by tool path, day and traffic-source category. This helps us understand which tools visitors find through search. It does not create visitor profiles or count unique people.</p>
    <p>We rely on legitimate interest for this limited audience measurement, subject to the applicable LGPD requirements. The <a href="https://www.gov.br/anpd/pt-br/centrais-de-conteudo/materiais-educativos-e-publicacoes/guia_orientativo_cookies_e_protecao_de_dados_pessoais">ANPD cookie guidance</a> says this basis may apply to audience measurement in some contexts when it is limited to aggregated patterns, without profiling or combining tracking mechanisms. Our assessment is documented in the repository; this notice explains the safeguards and the available opt-out.</p>

    <h2>Data and safeguards</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The analytics database keeps only date, site, tool path, pageview totals and a traffic-source category (direct, organic search, social, referral, campaign or internal).</li>
      <li>No cookies, browser IDs, device fingerprints or unique-person counts are used. Query strings and URL fragments are stripped; a campaign is recorded only as a yes/no category.</li>
      <li>The browser reduces a referrer to its origin, and the service immediately converts that origin to a source category. Raw referrers are not stored.</li>
      <li>Pageview aggregates are deleted after 400 days. Secret Sender reader links are excluded.</li>
      <li>Access logs are disabled for the Tools and Repasses web servers and the collector. The analytics application does not store IP addresses or user-agent strings, and those headers are not forwarded to the collector.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choice</h2>
    <p>You can disable future browser events with “Disable aggregate metrics” in the footer. The choice is stored only in your browser's local storage so it can be remembered; if you clear site data, you may need to disable it again. Already-counted aggregate pageviews cannot be linked back to your browser or removed individually.</p>

    <h2>Network providers</h2>
    <p>Requests pass through Cloudflare and the VM network. Those providers necessarily process connection details such as an IP address to deliver traffic, under their own terms and operational settings. The analytics database does not retain those connection details.</p>

    <h2>Secret Sender</h2>
    <p>Secret Sender reader links are excluded from analytics so their unguessable link IDs are not recorded. Its encrypted payload and file metadata are handled as described on the <a href="/secret/">Secret Sender page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
